; Every declaration carries the slot, so that `repr` and `interrupt` cost no
; grammar when the target that wants them arrives (`D-110`). What decides
; whether an annotation may sit there is the annotation, and `deprecated` warns
; at a use the compiler resolves by name — a `fn`, an `extern` or a `const`.
(struct (deprecated) Legacy ((value i64)))

(fn main () -> i32 0)
